3.text:
{B2} 

The position features three black groups whose liberties intersect at B2: {A2} (libs A1/A3/B2), {B3-B4} (libs A3/A4/B2) and {C1-C2} (libs B1/B2). White B2 is the sole point that simultaneously fills a liberty of each group, placing {A2} and {C1-C2} in atari while also reducing {B3-B4}. Any black reply (A3, B1, A1 or A4) leaves at least one group with a single remaining liberty that White fills on the next move, after which the surviving black stones have neither eyes nor an escape route.  

B1 only ataris {C1-C2}; Black can answer at B2, capture the atari stone and reconnect toward A1, restoring an extra liberty. All other candidates (A3, A1, C5, D3, …) leave at least one black group an extra liberty or connection, allowing Black to live or run out. Thus B2 is the unique forcing first move that initiates unconditional capture regardless of Black’s replies.

